    <string name="midi_help_firmware_link">Read about custom firmware</string>
    <string name="midi_help_find">The app can\'t find the Launchpad</string>
    <string name="midi_help_find_body">• Push the cable all the way in and use an adapter that fits your phone. Try another cable too.\n• The Launchpad is powered over USB. If it doesn\'t light up or only blinks, check the power first.\n• Your phone must support USB OTG (connecting external USB devices). If a window asks which app should use the USB device, choose UniPad.</string>
    <string name="midi_help_press">Connected, but pressing pads does nothing</string>
    <string name="midi_help_press_body">1. Press any pad and watch whether the status changes to “Pad signal received.”\n2. Check that the device in the status is your Launchpad. If the model is wrong, choose the right one in the model list. If your model isn\'t listed, don\'t pick another model in its place.\n3. If you changed the Launchpad\'s mode after connecting, unplug it and plug it in again. If you use custom firmware, see the guidance below.</string>
    <string name="midi_help_lights">Sound plays, but no lights</string>
    <string name="midi_help_lights_body">• Some packs have no light data. Check with a pack that has lights.\n• Launchpad X and Mini MK3 may start with the lights off.\n• Lights being off alone doesn\'t mean the connection failed.</string>
    <string name="midi_help_wrong">The wrong pad responds</string>
    <string name="midi_help_wrong_body">• If the chosen model differs from your Launchpad, pads land in the wrong place. Compare the device in the status with the chosen model.\n• The Launchpad may have switched to another mode (for example Live mode). Unplug it and plug it in again.\n• If you use custom firmware, see “I use custom firmware” below.</string>
    <string name="midi_help_chain">Right-side buttons don\'t change chains</string>
    <string name="midi_help_chain_body">Check in this order.\n1. While the option window is open on the play screen, the right-side buttons change the volume. Close the option window. The 4th button from the left on the top row opens and closes it.\n2. The 8 right-side buttons are chains 1–8 from the top. Buttons below the pack\'s number of chains do nothing.\n3. If it still doesn\'t work, unplug the Launchpad and plug it in again.</string>
    <string name="midi_help_firmware">I use custom firmware</string>
    <string name="midi_help_firmware_body">• UniPad recognises “Launchpad Open” for the Launchpad Pro (first model) and CoreFW. When it does, the status shows “Custom firmware”.\n• Only if you know the installed firmware is CoreFW or Launchpad Open, choose “Launchpad (CoreFW)” or “Launchpad Pro (Launchpad Open)” in the model list yourself. Choosing it does not confirm the firmware.\n• UniPad doesn\'t promise that every feature works with custom firmware, and it doesn\'t install or change firmware.</string>
    <string name="midi_help_crash">The app closes unexpectedly</string>
    <string name="midi_help_crash_body">Disconnect the device and note the app version, phone or tablet model, operating system, and the step where it closed. You do not need to repeat the crash.</string>
