    <string name="midi_help_apps_play">How do I play with another app on this phone?</string>
    <string name="midi_help_apps_play_body">1. Open the other app, such as a Launchpad emulator, and keep it running.\n2. Here, under “Apps on this phone”, pick its device, check the ports and the model, then tap “Connect”.\n3. Show both apps side by side in split screen (in Recents, tap the app\'s icon and choose split screen), then open a pack in UniPad.\n• Pads pressed in the other window keep playing while UniPad\'s play screen is visible. Home, locking the phone or another full-screen app stops the sound.\n• Split screen needs support from both your phone and the other app. Where either doesn\'t offer it, UniPad can\'t keep playing beside it.</string>
    <string name="midi_help_apps_missing">The app isn\'t in the list</string>
    <string name="midi_help_apps_missing_body">• Open the other app first. Some apps offer their MIDI device only while they run.\n• Tap “Search again”. UniPad reads the list only when you ask.\n• Bluetooth and network MIDI devices aren\'t listed here.</string>
